<title>VIETNAM: Kyoei Steel in Vietnam deepwater port project.</title>
<headline>Kyoei Steel in Vietnam deepwater port project.</headline>
<dateline>HANOI 1997-05-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vietnam has approved a venture between Japan's Kyoei Steel and two state-owned firms to build a $56 million deepwater port in the southern province of Ba Gia-Vung Tau, a project official said on Saturday.</p>
<p>Le Van Long, director of the Vung Tau Sea Transport and Service Company, said Kyoei Steel would have a 52 percent share in the Thi Vai port project.</p>
<p>His company would take 25.6 percent of the equity and Vietnam Steel Corporation would have the remaining 22.4 percent.</p>
<p>The port will be capable of accomodating container vessels of 30,000-50,000 tonnes.</p>
</text>
